    LLM: 'Game: Thuni (Nigerian). Plain-trick game, J-9-A-10-K-Q ranking. Follow suit; win majority of tricks. Partnership.',
    Player: 'Nigerian Thuni is a trick-taking game related to South African Thunee but played as a plain-trick game (no card points). The objective is winning tricks rather than counting card values, though the unusual ranking (J-9 high) remains.',
    objective: 'Win the majority of tricks. No card points are counted; the game is played as plain-trick with the unusual ranking J-9-A-10-K-Q. Partners sit opposite and combine trick counts.',
    gameplay: 'Dealer deals all cards (6 each with 24-card deck or 8 each with 32-card deck). Left of dealer leads to the first trick. Players must follow suit when able; otherwise may play any card. Highest card of the led suit wins the trick; trick winner leads next. Game ends when all tricks are played; side with more tricks wins.',
